## Key Components to Implement

### 1. `NotificationManager` (`app/backend/notifier.py`)
* Wraps `QSystemTrayIcon` from `PySide6.QtWidgets`.
* Methods:
  * `notify_error(title, message)`: Triggers native OS warning/critical notification.
  * `notify_success(title, message)`: Triggers recovery/success notification.
  * `notify_info(title, message)`: General notifications.
* Works seamlessly on Windows 10/11 (Action Center / Toasts) and macOS (Notification Center).

### 2. `BrokerHealthMonitor` (`app/backend/broker_monitor.py`)
* Runs in a dedicated background worker thread with configurable polling frequency (default: every 5-10 seconds).
* Maintains lightweight SSH connections/heartbeat probes to each broker host (`host:port`).
* Detects transition states:
  * `CONNECTED` (🟢 Active SSH & responsive).
  * `SSH_DROPPED` (🔴 Connection timeout / socket closed / auth failure).
  * `RECONNECTED` (🟢 Automatic recovery detected).
* Emits Qt signals:
  * `brokerStatusChanged(int nodeId, str host, str status, str errorMsg)`
  * `connectionAlert(str title, str message, str level)`

### 3. Backend Integration (`app/backend/controller.py` & `app/main.py`)
* `app/main.py`: Updated to use `QApplication` and initialize the system tray icon.
* `app/backend/controller.py`:
  * Spawns/updates `BrokerHealthMonitor` whenever `brokers` list is refreshed.
  * Listens for `connectionAlert` and forwards to `NotificationManager`.
  * Logs disconnection events into SQLite `activity_logs`.
  * Enriches broker model with `ssh_status` (e.g. `"CONNECTED"`, `"UNREACHABLE"`).

